<title>NEW ZEALAND: F&amp;P year profit falls 5.3 percent.</title>
<headline>F&amp;P year profit falls 5.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year result to March 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				  37. 16 vs 39.25</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 33.0 vs 36.0</p>
<p>    Final div (cents)			  9.0 vs 9.0</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)		18.0 vs 18.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				  781.38 vs 816.64</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    55.00 vs 57.28</p>
<p>    Tax					  17.84 vs 19.27</p>
<p>    Equity earnings			   nil  vs 1.24</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	113.73 vs 110.75</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Aug 1</p>
<p>Reg date July 17</p>
<p>Ex div   July 21</p>
<p>Note - Fisher and Paykel Industries Ltd is a domestic appliance manufacturer.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
